course: dictionary
lesson: 421
title: Approve: three meanings in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word approve has three main meanings, and the context tells you which one fits. It can mean you think something is good, you officially say yes to a plan, or you check something and accept it. Ask yourself: is someone giving a good opinion, or giving permission?
explain: «The head teacher approved the trip to the museum.» The head said yes to a plan, so approve means officially allow it. Now try your meaning in the sentence: "The head teacher officially said yes to the trip." It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: «The animals did not hold with villages.» The dictionary says this means they did not approve of them. The clue is "did not", so approve of is the opposite of disliking something. Approve of means you think something is good or right.
fact: Approve means to think something is good or right, or to officially say yes to it.
fact: Approve of means you like or agree with a person, a plan or an idea.
fact: Approve a plan means you officially allow it to happen.
fact: A seal of approval is a sign that something has been checked and accepted.
fact: Some medicines are not approved for younger children, so pharmacists check the age on the packet.
exercise: «The head teacher approved the trip to the zoo.» What does approved mean here? | To lose | To be very tired | *Officially said yes to | Painted green
exercise: Mum says, «I approve of your new library book choice.» What does approve of mean? | To throw it away | To pay for the book | To forget the book | *To think it is a good choice
exercise: Find and copy the phrase that means a sign that something has been checked and accepted. | new friend | head teacher | *seal of approval | zoo trip
test: «The council approved the plan for a new park.» What does approved mean? | *Officially agreed to it | Hid it from everyone | Made a loud noise about | Copied it exactly
test: «Ella does not approve of late nights, so she goes to bed at eight.» What does approve of suggest? | Is very hungry | *Thinks late nights are not a good idea | Loves staying up late | Has lost her bed
exam: «The bank approved my loan.» What does approved mean? | *To officially agree and allow it | To walk away quickly | To hide the money | To count the coins
